{"lines":[{"h":0.015833414128396339,"c":1,"y":0.048455452802367627,"w":0.082927900950113931,"t":"Reading","x":0.831317871657129},{"c":1,"y":0.095870206235650568,"h":0.017501886756019269,"t":"Analysing the trends in each variable, the researchers discovered that species with","x":0.080082134777082384,"w":0.78028747558593747},{"c":1,"t":"more flexible lifecycles were more likely to be able to benefit from an earlier emergence","y":0.11271281884273965,"x":0.080018010534879044,"w":0.81942891438802101,"h":0.018525654165442274},{"x":0.080082136097433934,"t":"driven by climate change. Some species are able to go from caterpillar to butterfly twice","w":0.82135523478190098,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"y":0.13215339209280486},{"h":0.023935787234686035,"x":0.079944529522589777,"w":0.79080993652343745,"c":1,"y":0.14552221666476839,"t":"or more per year, so that the individual butterflies you see flying in the spring are the"},{"t":"grandchildren or great-grandchildren of the individuals seen a year previously.","c":1,"y":0.16585669862843588,"x":0.079995331634894834,"w":0.73319620768229166,"h":0.019377707872418881},{"w":0.79064509073893241,"h":0.019370512835747422,"x":0.077989637228944933,"t":"Among these species, researchers observed that those which have been advancing","y":0.20197154959462149,"c":1},{"w":0.83367558797200525,"y":0.22093023267383027,"x":0.078028735688115108,"t":"their phenology the most over the 20-year study period also had the most positive trends","c":1,"h":0.015988371857499684},{"y":0.2368806845001159,"t":"in abundance, distribution and northwards extent. For these species, such as Britain's","c":1,"w":0.807082265218099,"h":0.020128658598503213,"x":0.077980502255424258},{"t":"tiniest butterfly, the dainty Small Blue, whose colonies are up to a hundred strong, some","h":0.017503601119229772,"c":1,"x":0.078028766420350171,"w":0.82546198527018233,"y":0.25575221263367065},{"t":"develop into butterflies early in spring, allowing their summer generations to complete","c":1,"w":0.80287470499674474,"x":0.080082156459533094,"y":0.27315634243591491,"h":0.017541331738497146},{"h":0.016224188790560312,"t":"another reproductive cycle by autumn so that more population growth occurs.","c":1,"y":0.29203539808569268,"w":0.72895278930664065,"x":0.080082127183940019},{"w":0.79487965901692692,"t":"Other species, however, are less flexible and restricted to a single reproductive cycle","x":0.079987659576504194,"c":1,"h":0.022193800664580987,"y":0.32479749951700532},{"t":"per year. For these species, there was no evidence of any benefit to emerging earlier.","w":0.80287475585937496,"x":0.080082129192427756,"y":0.34447674467973777,"h":0.018945084068275775,"c":1},{"t":"Indeed, worryingly, it was found that the species in this group that specialise in very","h":0.018020628757533075,"c":1,"x":0.077985957938223008,"y":0.36294960876674665,"w":0.78448476155598956},{"h":0.018904781060232856,"x":0.080082136882917515,"y":0.37935103220708555,"c":1,"w":0.78850102742513017,"t":"specific habitat types, often related to the caterpillar's preferred diet, actually tended"},{"c":1,"t":"to be most at harm from advancing phenology. The beautiful High Brown Fritillary,","x":0.078028771652292148,"y":0.39823008822956418,"w":0.77002049763997393,"h":0.01746758598845255},{"t":"often described as Britain's most endangered butterfly, is in this group. It is found only","x":0.08001416602222397,"y":0.4150000804230104,"w":0.8050692749023437,"h":0.019366133248208128,"c":1},{"x":0.078028760078612716,"w":0.80082132975260412,"t":"in coppiced woodland and limestone pavement habitats. It is also a single-generation","y":0.43451327425545816,"h":0.016068120973300126,"c":1},{"y":0.45199135064634621,"c":1,"x":0.080037407566135532,"t":"butterfly that has advanced its phenology. This suggests that climate change, while","w":0.77832870483398442,"h":0.018883391748839018},{"w":0.82956878662109379,"y":0.47079645992582542,"x":0.080082136349770863,"h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1,"t":"undoubtedly not the sole cause, might have played a part in the downfall of this species."},{"h":0.020851745155356927,"w":0.80710255940755204,"c":1,"x":0.080008483286827831,"t":"All is not lost, however. Many of Britain's single-generation species show the capacity,","y":0.50314750850496448},{"y":0.52325581397066701,"t":"in continental Europe, to add a second generation in years that are sufficiently warm.","x":0.078028760251240878,"w":0.80082132975260412,"h":0.017452150530519739,"c":1},{"w":0.82135523478190109,"x":0.080082136100067869,"c":1,"y":0.54215116281467024,"h":0.017441860412777732,"t":"Therefore, as the climate continues to warm, species like the Silver-studded Blue might"},{"c":1,"x":0.080082134610803074,"t":"be able to switch to multiple generations in the UK as well, and so begin to extract","y":0.55958702047477282,"w":0.77207392374674477,"h":0.017447863215893755},{"c":1,"w":0.74548685709635409,"t":"benefits from the additional warmth, potentially leading to population increases.","y":0.57669879001307445,"h":0.020047098345461145,"x":0.080026277257186779},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"x":0.080082147117183047,"t":"More immediately, conservationists can arm themselves with all this knowledge to","y":0.61327433617632454,"w":0.76796712239583331},{"x":0.080082141494362602,"w":0.79055440266927079,"t":"spot the warning signs of species that may be at risk. The White Admiral of southern","y":0.63067846592939802,"h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1},{"y":0.64745095265328134,"x":0.080024904635566066,"h":0.019283164145320608,"c":1,"t":"England, a much sought-after butterfly, experienced a significant increase in numbers","w":0.80300684611002604},{"w":0.82146352132161438,"c":1,"t":"from the 1920s but has shown a considerable decline in the past 20 years. This may be","y":0.66544095297306693,"x":0.080030881244738061,"h":0.019262053903225218},{"t":"because the caterpillar exists solely on a diet of a plant called honeysuckle. But it is also","x":0.0800821300295676,"w":0.82751541137695317,"y":0.68459302336857941,"h":0.015996947049391252,"c":1},{"t":"likely to be due to climate change.","x":0.077941911064676975,"y":0.70219685248197428,"h":0.017537877130649027,"w":0.32665158589680993,"c":1},{"y":0.9244186048926486,"w":0.02669404347737625,"h":0.013081394746943587,"c":1,"t":"85","x":0.88706365579537949},{"y":0.94166666658950615,"h":0.04166666666666663,"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51176469618764042,"w":0.45882354736328113}],"w":2400,"h":3390}